---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config';

const title = 'Account & data deletion | Quorivell';
const mailto = `mailto:${siteConfig.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Delete my account')}`;
---

<SiteLayout
  title={title}
  description="How to delete your Quorivell account and data in the Android app or by email, including the 30-day grace period."
>
  <section class="document shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">Account &amp; data deletion</div>
    <h1>Delete your<br /><em>account.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Quorivell is the Android app from Quorivell. You can delete your account in the app, or request the same deletion by email if the app is no longer installed.
    </p>

    <a class="contact-card" href={mailto}>
      <span class="section-label">Request deletion by email</span>
      <strong>{siteConfig.email}</strong>
      <span>Subject: Delete my account <span aria-hidden="true">-&gt;</span></span>
    </a>

    <div class="policy-grid">
      <aside>
        <span class="section-label">Developer</span>
        <p>Quorivell · Android app · {siteConfig.email}</p>
      </aside>
      <article>
        <h2>In the app</h2>
        <p>
          Open <strong>Account</strong>, then tap <strong>Delete account</strong>. You must be signed in. The app asks you to confirm, then marks your account and all cloud data for deletion, deletes the ledger on that device, and signs you out.
        </p>

        <h2>Without the app</h2>
        <p>
          If you cannot use the app, email <a href={mailto}>{siteConfig.email}</a> from the address of your Quorivell account. Use the subject line <strong>Delete my account</strong>. Do not send your password. We verify the request, start the same deletion process described below, and confirm by email.
        </p>

        <h2>30-day grace period</h2>
        <p>
          A deletion request starts a 30-day grace period. Your account and cloud data are marked for deletion immediately. You can restore them by signing in again within 30 days. After a restore, the app shows a welcome-back message and brings your cloud records back onto the device.
        </p>

        <h2>Permanent purge</h2>
        <p>
          After 30 days, a daily automated job permanently deletes all associated cloud data: your login, Firestore documents under your account (including settings and synced records), and profile photos in Firebase Storage. Because the job runs once a day, data is gone within about one day after the grace period ends. This cannot be undone.
        </p>

        <h2>Data that stays on a device</h2>
        <p>
          Source conversations and chats are stored on the device and are not uploaded with cloud sync. Deleting your account also clears the ledger on the device you used. You can wipe local records independently at any time: <strong>Account</strong> -> <strong>Delete ledger on this device</strong>. That action does not delete your account or cloud copies. Uninstalling the app removes remaining on-device files.
        </p>

        <h2>Delete cloud data only</h2>
        <p>
          If you want to keep the account, signed-in users can tap <strong>Delete all cloud data</strong> on the Account screen. Cloud copies are marked deleted and purged after 30 days. You stay signed in, and data on the device is kept.
        </p>

        <p class="updated">Last updated: October 11, 2026</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
